  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">transboundary collaboration, law enforcement and tourism development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to reduce the trafficking of elephant ivory in Lao PDR. Specific activities will include: review, update, and distribute training tools for use by enforcement officers; conduct a multi-agency training for inspection and enforcement officers situated at key transit and trade locations; conduct an illegal ivory trade awareness campaign at key border ports; conduct targeted multi-agency patrols of key border and transit locations; assist the government to report required information to CITES, MIKE, and ETIS. This project will contribute to the strengthening of the control of ivory trafficking in Lao PDR.</narrative>
  </description>
